        title       Lane policies: latest, serialize and cancel, and endings split by origin (slice 1)
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T54]
        satisfies   [@plan.Operations.O3, @plan.Runtime.O2]
        description
            Build the write-lane policies `latest`, `serialize` (up to 64, then Overloaded) and `cancel` on production,
            with the `waiting` row, as rows of the lane table, and endings split by origin.

            **Why now:** production refuses every policy but `reject`.

            **Read first:** @spec.WriteLanes, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/cells.ts#table, and the
            reference `packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/round-14/lane.ts`.

            May change: `src/core/`, `fixtures/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a policy whose cells are right one at a time but wrong in sequence → caught by generated Stories
            over a fixture that uses each policy.
        acceptance
            - Each policy's cells are rows of the lane table, with a Story test for each decided cell and a fixture that
              uses the policy.
            - An operation's row reads `waiting` while commits wait behind its head.
            - Each new rule has a planted fault that `nub run faults` catches.
